    "turn_text": "I know that's kind of difficult to understand, but that was audio from just a couple of days ago. Senator Arlen Specter speaking before the Allegheny County Democratic Club thanking the Allegheny County Republicans for endorsing him. for Senate. I guess there's a problem when you've been a Republican for so many years and then you decide to switch parties and add on to it, you know, being a little further up in years and not remembering what party you belong to, you know, just one of the clues to show that maybe it's time for Arlen Specter to go home. The other clue is when you've got a really good progressive challenger who can take over and further the cause, it really is time to go home. Well, that challenger is with us now. Congressman Joe Sestak of Pennsylvania has mounted a primary challenge to Arlen Specter. The primary in Pennsylvania is coming up this Tuesday and it's a very tight race and Congressman Joe Sestak joins us right now on the Randy Rhodes Show. Congressman, thanks so much for being with us today.",
