    "turn_text": "I think the principle compromise is, look, We've got to secure the border. And I say that as head of the Navy's anti-terrorism unit, because I know that south of the border, our alcata, very far south, involved the narco trade. So it isn't just illegal immigration. We've got to first secure the borders. Second, we've got to, while we're doing that, do set up a system where you can very readily check if someone's here legally. But third, and simultaneously, as you're doing that, you've given opportunity for the 11 and 12 million who are here legally to come out of the shadows. And they get to the back of the line.",
